Hello everyone!

In this patch note, we'll be covering some of the changes that happened throughout the game since its release, from 1.0.0 through 1.1.0.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Level Design[/h2]
After the initial release, we got a lot of feedback from players about certain areas of the game that we've since changed. These include:
[list]
[*] Made the last level of the Jungle chapter significantly easier and more forgiving.
[*] Improved many levels in the Underground chapter, especially near the end. Those levels include:
 ▪ The blue flower room before the elevator;
 ▪ The second room on the mushroom section of the Fortress;
 ▪ The second-to-last room on the blue flower section of the Fortress;
 ▪ The key room on the water flower section of the Fortress;
 ▪ The second room on the yellow flower section of the Fortress;
 ▪ The key room on the green flower section of the Fortress;
[*] Improved decorations and visuals of the Fortress in the Underground chapter;
[*] Updated the two Easter Egg rooms (if you know, you know).
[/list]

[h2]Gameplay[/h2]
[list]
[*] Included target times for the Underground chapter medals;
[*] Fixed a bug where players would get stuck in-between two rooms in the Jungle chapter;
[*] Made ice slippery, as was the original intent (but this doesn't affect gameplay much);
[*] Added many checkpoints, tweaked many existing ones. Progression should feel more fair;
[*] Improved the presentation of fake emeralds in the Easter Egg room (if you know, you know).
[/list]

[h2]Bugfixes and Optimization[/h2]
[list]
[*] Fixed a bug where players would randomly teleport to the top of certain blocks and platforms, and get stuck inside walls;
[*] Fixed some places where players could fall through jumpthrough platforms and die or get stuck;
[*] Fixed a room transition issue in the Home (epilogue) chapter.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

We might have missed a couple of changes – not counting the many tiny tweaks we didn't mention. But if you find anything else, have any feedback, bug reports, or just want to chat, you can reach out to us on our [url=https://discord.gg/ehpFwJESvz]official Discord server[/url]. We're also on [url=https://twitter.com/Gagonfe]Twitter @Gagonfe[/url] and [url=https://twitter.com/HugoBDesigner]Twitter @HugoBDesigner[/url].

Thank you for reading this patch note, thank you for playing our game, and thank you for being awesome! Happy Archaeogaming!

Hello all, and welcome to another update for the Archaeogem Demo!

This time around, we have implemented many improvements, bugfixes and features to the game based on your feedback since the last major update. While this is a smaller update, we have made a whole host of changes to ensure players have their best time playing Archaeogem!

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Level Design[/h2]
For starters, we have improved and refined the gameplay in both the tutorial and the crystal areas, given the feedback from the community. Among these changes are:
[list]
[*] Visual improvements to the tutorial area;
[*] Small visual tweaks to the crystal area;
[*] More intuitive gameplay for the bridge section of the crystal biome;
[*] More intuitive gameplay for the final room of the crystal biome.
[/list]

[h2]Gameplay[/h2]
Secondly, we have heard several comments regarding certain recurring gameplay issues and have taken some time to address them. Those are:
[list]
[*] Overhauled moving platforms, which now transfer momentum more accurately and fairly, and also accelerate and decelerate;
[*] Fixed bug where the player would die if a falling platform with spikes respawned on top of the player;
[*] Crouching player sprite now looks lower as to indicate the changing player height more clearly;
[*] Player looking up now has a higher visibility range;
[*] Dialogue speeches can now be sped up by holding the skip dialogue button.
[/list]

On top of that, we have also added a timer for speedrunners, and made some changes to the in-game UI:
[list]
[*] It is now possible to enable an on-screen timer for completing a chapter;
[*] The pause menu now shows your current gameplay time for that chapter;
[*] All gameplay settings can now be accessed through the pause menu, including controller settings;
[*] Controller settings now show the movement buttons;
[*] When the game is paused, it is possible to hold down the dash button to hide the pause menu;
[*] Now you can restart the chapter via the pause menu even when the player is dead.
[/list]

[h2]Save slots[/h2]
Save slots have been massively improved, making them more intuitive to use, and also integrated them with the new gameplay timer. We have:
[list]
[*] Slots look and feel better, with improved animations and clearer display of information;
[*] They now show the correct information pertaining to the demo area;
[*] Slots will now show you the total gameplay time for that save. [b]Important:[/b] players who had saves before this update will have their initial timer set to 0.
[/list]

[h2]Bugfixes and Optimization[/h2]
We have also worked to improve the overall gameplay experience by taking in and resolving bug reports sent by players. Those include:
[list]
[*] Fixed a bug where parts of the player's progress were kept even when the chapter was restarted;
[*] Fixed the bug where the credits would roll infinitely;
[*] Improved performance in some of the levels.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

We're still hard at work on the upcoming chapters, new game mechanics, and more. You can reach out to us if you have suggestions, feedback, bug reports, or if you just want to share your experience with Archaeogem. We're over on [url=https://twitter.com/Gagonfe]Twitter @Gagonfe[/url].

Thank you for reading! Stay tuned for more updates and news, and happy archaeologing!
